cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Automat, please cite this software and the associated research paper."
title: "Automat: Autoresearch Workflow for Designing Chemical Composition Descriptors"
type: software
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: 2026-08-04

authors:
  - family-names: "Cobelli"
    given-names: "Matteo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6829-2754"
    affiliation: "School of Physics and CRANN Institute, Trinity College Dublin"

abstract: >-
  Automat is a minimal autoresearch framework for designing composition-only
  descriptors for materials-property regression tasks. A coding agent proposes,
  implements, evaluates, and refines chemically motivated descriptors within a
  reproducible random-forest workflow.

repository-code: "https://github.com/m-cobelli/automat"
url: "https://github.com/m-cobelli/automat"
license: "MIT"

keywords:
  - materials science
  - materials informatics
  - compositional descriptors
  - machine learning
  - autoresearch
  - agentic AI
